-- P4, package H5 (docs/specs/p4-nodes.md 5.6 and 9.2, T-542): what the hub knows of a node's return and drain, for the admin page.
--
-- The F3 conditions that keep a withdrawn node out and the drain of a node that stopped being advertised are
-- worked out from the trackers in the hub's memory (the Heartbeats, the prober, the table it signed), which no
-- other process has. 0100 persisted only the failover columns, so the node page could say "withdrawn" and
-- nothing of why or how long. The hub now writes the two facts here when they change (not on every tick), and
-- the admin reads them into NodeView. The row is a view of the hub's state and never an input of it: the hub
